    "created_at": "2019-10-25T05:54:39Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-10-25T05:54:39Z",
    "body": "We just had a security hole pointed out on a user content domain that only exists because of AppCache, especially in Chromium with its CHROMIUM-INTERCEPT feature. This whole AppCache thing was supposed to be an optional enhancement, and it’s long obsolete, and everyone supports Service Workers for at least a year and a half now; so any chance of stirring up discussion towards killing it outright at last?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
